# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in when David has real keys.
# Emulator picks this up automatically (Firebase Functions v2 dotenv convention).
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  BEFORE YOU PASTE A KEY: WHAT EACH VENDOR DOES WITH THIS FAMILY'S FINANCIAL DATA
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Filling in a key below is the moment this stops being a local app. The three keys here are the
#  only thing standing between the mock adapter and real bank statements, real salaries and real
#  family members' names leaving this machine — the AI settings screen and every send surface
#  disclose WHAT leaves; this file is the only place that can tell you WHO KEEPS IT.
#
#  A key left blank is the safest setting there is: with no key the provider is not offered at all
#  and the mock adapter answers locally, with nothing sent anywhere.
#
#  ── HOW FAR TO TRUST WHAT FOLLOWS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  Checked against each vendor's own published page on 2026-08-18, against the LIVE pages, and
#  each claim below is one those pages state directly. That is not the same as a guarantee:
#  vendor terms change without notice, and this file cannot know when they have. TREAT THE DATE
#  AS AN EXPIRY, NOT A SIGNATURE — re-read the linked page before trusting any line here, and
#  especially before pointing a key at anything you would not want a stranger to read.
#
#  Deliberately NOT recorded here: anything about enterprise agreements, DPAs, zero-retention
#  addenda or regional data residency. Those are contract terms this project has never seen, and
#  a plausible-sounding sentence about a contract nobody has read is the same defect as the
#  unverified rate card the AI settings screen now carries a caveat about. Where a page did not
#  answer a question, this file says so instead of guessing.
#
#  ── ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (Claude Opus 5, Claude Sonnet 5 — chat, insight) ───────────────────────
#
#    Training:  NOT by default. Anthropic's page states: "By default, we will not use your inputs
#               or outputs from our commercial products (e.g. Claude for Work, Anthropic API,
#               Claude Gov, etc.) to train our models." Consent is the exception — notably the
#               thumbs-up/down feedback control, which this app does not implement and must not
#               grow one without revisiting this line.
#    Retention: NOT ANSWERED by that page for ordinary API traffic. It gives a figure only for
#               feedback you explicitly submit (up to 5 years) and refers the general question to
#               the Trust Center and the Commercial Terms. Unresolved, and recorded as unresolved.
#    Opt out:   nothing to opt out of for training on the default path. Do NOT submit feedback on
#               a response that contains family financial data.
#    Check:     https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/7996868-is-my-data-used-for-model-training
#               https://trust.anthropic.com/  ·  https://www.anthropic.com/legal/commercial-terms
#
#  ── OPENAI_API_KEY (GPT-5.1 — chat) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#    Training:  NOT by default. OpenAI's page states that "data sent to the OpenAI API is not used
#               to train or improve OpenAI models (unless you explicitly opt in to share data with
#               us)", in effect since 2023-03-01.
#    Retention: up to 30 days of abuse-monitoring logs containing customer content, "unless longer
#               retention is required by law". Some stateful endpoints (Assistants, vector stores)
#               keep data until it is deleted; this app uses neither.
#    Opt out:   a Zero Data Retention control exists that excludes content from those logs, but it
#               is NOT self-serve — it is "subject to prior approval by OpenAI and acceptance of
#               additional requirements", arranged through their sales team.
#    Check:     https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data
#
#  ── GEMINI_API_KEY (Gemini 3 Flash — DOCUMENT EXTRACTION) ────────────────────────────────────
#
#    ⚠ READ THIS ONE BEFORE THE OTHER TWO. It is the only key here whose default answer is "yes,
#      they train on it", and it is also the key that drives DOCUMENT EXTRACTION — the path that
#      sends whole bank statements and invoices, and the path the unattended whole-folder sync
#      runs once per file without a human watching.
#
#    Training:  DEPENDS ENTIRELY ON WHETHER THE KEY IS ON A BILLED PROJECT.
#               · Unpaid / free tier — YES. Google's terms state that "Google uses the content you
#                 submit to the Services and any generated responses to provide, improve, and
#                 develop Google products", and that "human reviewers may read, annotate, and
#                 process your API input and output". Google says such data is disconnected from
#                 the Google Account, API key and Cloud project before reviewers see it. It does
#                 not say the CONTENT is redacted, and a bank statement identifies a family
#                 perfectly well without an account id attached to it.
#               · Paid tier — NO. "Google doesn't use your prompts or responses to improve our
#                 products."
#    Retention: paid tier, up to 30 days, "solely for detecting and preventing violations of the
#               Prohibited Use Policy". No retention period is stated for the free tier.
#    Opt out:   there is no opt-out toggle. THE BILLING STATUS *IS* THE SETTING — putting the key
#               on a billed Cloud project is what moves it to the paid terms. If this key is on a
#               free-tier project, treat every document extracted through it as published.
#    Check:     https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms
#
#  ── IF NONE OF THAT IS ACCEPTABLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  Leave the key blank. The mock adapter is always available, never leaves the machine, and the
#  egress notices say so explicitly rather than going quiet.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
